BT /F2 16 Tf 54 723 Td (TesseraCloud Regional Failover Runbook) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 701 Td (Document ID: eng-tesseracloud-failover-runbook) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 679 Td (Owner: Platform Engineering \(Head: Kofi Mensah-Bonsu\)) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 657 Td (Last reviewed: 2025-06-20) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 635 Td (Version: 3.2) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 613 Td (Classification: Internal. Applies to TesseraCloud production only.) Tj ET
BT /F2 13 Tf 54 588 Td (1. Purpose and scope) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 566 Td (This runbook describes how to move TesseraCloud production traffic from the primary region euw1) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 553 Td (\(Dublin\) to the secondary disaster recovery region euc1 \(Frankfurt\), how to verify the result,) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 540 Td (and how to fail back once the primary region is healthy again. It covers the customer-facing) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 527 Td (services that make up the TesseraCloud SaaS platform: the telemetry ingestion tier that) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 514 Td (receives data from TS-4 gateways and TS-4e edge nodes, the public API and web application, the) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 501 Td (stream processing tier, the Kafka event backbone and the TimescaleDB time-series store.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 479 Td (The runbook does not cover the Atlas ERP integration \(billing export\), which is batch based and) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 466 Td (is re-run manually after a failover, and it does not cover the on-premises TS-4 gateway fleet) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 453 Td (itself, which requires no action from Meridian during a failover because gateways reconnect by) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 440 Td (DNS name.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 418 Td (The recovery objectives committed to customers in the TesseraCloud service description are:) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 396 Td (- Recovery Time Objective \(RTO\): 60 minutes from the failover decision to restored ingestion) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 383 Td (   and API service in euc1.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 370 Td (- Recovery Point Objective \(RPO\): 5 minutes of telemetry at most, measured at the Kafka and) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 357 Td (   TimescaleDB layers.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 344 Td (Because TS-4 gateways buffer telemetry locally, the effective customer data loss in most) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 331 Td (failovers is zero; the RPO applies to data that had already been acknowledged by tc-ingest in) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 318 Td (euw1 but had not yet been replicated to euc1.) Tj ET
BT /F2 13 Tf 54 293 Td (2. When to fail over) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 271 Td (A regional failover is a significant event. It moves every customer tenant, invalidates warm) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 258 Td (caches and requires a planned failback later. Do not fail over for a single degraded component) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 245 Td (that can be repaired in place within the RTO. Use the criteria below. If in doubt, the Incident) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 232 Td (Commander decides, and the decision is recorded in the incident channel.) Tj ET
BT /F2 9 Tf 54 211 Td (Situation | Fail over? | Notes) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 54 199 Td (Cloud provider declares a regional outage affecting euw1 compute or networking | Yes | Start at) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 54 187 Td (step 1 immediately; do not wait for provider ETA) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 54 175 Td (tc-ingest unavailable in all euw1 availability zones for more than 15 minutes with no) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 54 163 Td (identified fix | Yes | Check the tc-ingest health endpoint first \(step 4\)) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 54 151 Td (TimescaleDB primary and synchronous standby both lost | Yes | Regional failover is faster than) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 54 139 Td (rebuilding the primary) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 54 127 Td (Kafka cluster in euw1 has lost quorum or more than two brokers | Yes, unless the brokers are) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 54 115 Td (returning | Confirm with the Kafka on-call engineer) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 54 103 Td (Single broker, single database node or single availability zone lost | No | Handle with the) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 54 91 Td (component runbooks) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 54 79 Td (Elevated API latency or error rate under 5 percent | No | Treat as SEV2 or SEV3 per the) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 54 67 Td (severity definitions) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 54 55 Td (Security incident requiring isolation of euw1 | Case by case | Head of IT Security \(Mei-Ling) Tj ET
endstream
endobj
