BT /F1 9 Tf 54 730 Td (Tan\) must be consulted) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 708 Td (A failover is always handled as a SEV1 incident as defined in it-incident-severity-definitions,) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 695 Td (regardless of how the incident was originally classified. If the incident was opened at a lower) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 682 Td (severity, the Incident Commander raises it to SEV1 at the moment the failover decision is) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 669 Td (taken.) Tj ET
BT /F2 13 Tf 54 644 Td (3. Decision authority and roles) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 622 Td (The decision to fail over is made by the Incident Commander, with approval from the Head of) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 609 Td (Platform Engineering or the delegated duty manager listed on the Platform on-call rotation.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 596 Td (Approval may be given verbally on the incident bridge; the Incident Commander records the name) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 583 Td (of the approver and the time in the incident channel. If neither the Head of Platform) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 570 Td (Engineering nor the duty manager can be reached within 10 minutes, the Incident Commander may) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 557 Td (proceed alone and must note the attempts to reach them.) Tj ET
BT /F2 9 Tf 54 536 Td (Role | Filled by | Responsibilities) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 54 524 Td (Incident Commander \(IC\) | Platform on-call primary, or the senior engineer who declared the) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 54 512 Td (incident | Owns the decision, runs the bridge, keeps the timeline) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 54 500 Td (Approver | Head of Platform Engineering or delegated duty manager | Approves failover and) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 54 488 Td (failback) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 54 476 Td (Operator | Platform on-call secondary | Runs tcctl commands and records output) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 54 464 Td (Database lead | Data platform on-call | Promotes TimescaleDB, checks replication) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 54 452 Td (Kafka lead | Streaming on-call | Checks MirrorMaker 2, moves consumer groups) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 54 440 Td (Communications lead | Customer Support duty lead | Updates status page and key account contacts) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 54 428 Td (Scribe | Any available engineer | Keeps timestamps in the incident channel) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 406 Td (One person may hold several roles in a small incident, but the Incident Commander should never) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 393 Td (also be the Operator.) Tj ET
BT /F2 13 Tf 54 368 Td (4. Architecture summary) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 346 Td (TesseraCloud runs active-passive across two regions. Only euw1 serves customer traffic in) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 333 Td (normal operation. euc1 runs warm standby capacity: the Kubernetes services are deployed at) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 320 Td (reduced replica counts, the database replica is continuously applying changes, and MirrorMaker) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 307 Td (2 copies Kafka topics from euw1 to euc1.) Tj ET
BT /F2 9 Tf 54 286 Td (Component | Primary \(euw1\) | DR \(euc1\) | Port | Replication) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 54 274 Td (tc-ingest \(MQTT ingestion\) | tc-ingest deployment, 12 replicas | tc-ingest deployment, 3) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 54 262 Td (replicas \(scaled on failover\) | 8883 MQTT over TLS; 8081 health | Stateless) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 54 250 Td (tc-api \(public API and web\) | tc-api deployment, 8 replicas | tc-api deployment, 2 replicas |) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 54 238 Td (443 HTTPS | Stateless) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 54 226 Td (tc-stream \(Kafka consumers\) | consumer group tc-stream-prd | same group name, stopped until) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 54 214 Td (promotion | n/a | Offsets translated by MirrorMaker 2) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 54 202 Td (Kafka | kafka-prd-01 to kafka-prd-06 | kafka-dr-01 to kafka-dr-03 | 9093 TLS | MirrorMaker 2,) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 54 190 Td (asynchronous) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 54 178 Td (TimescaleDB primary | tsdb-prd-01.tessera.meridian.internal | n/a | 5432 | Synchronous to) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 54 166 Td (tsdb-prd-02) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 54 154 Td (TimescaleDB standby | tsdb-prd-02 \(synchronous\) | tsdb-dr-01.euc1.tessera.meridian.internal) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 54 142 Td (\(asynchronous\) | 5432 | Streaming replication) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 54 130 Td (Public DNS | ingest.tesseracloud.meridian-instruments.com,) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 54 118 Td (api.tesseracloud.meridian-instruments.com | same names, switched by tcctl | n/a | TTL 60) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 54 106 Td (seconds) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 84 Td (TS-4 gateways connect to ingest.tesseracloud.meridian-instruments.com on port 8883 using MQTT) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 71 Td (over TLS. TS-4e edge nodes normally forward through a TS-4 gateway; the small number of TS-4e) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 58 Td (units configured for direct cloud connection use the same DNS name and port. The public API and) Tj ET
endstream
