stream
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 729 Td (web application are reached at api.tesseracloud.meridian-instruments.com on port 443.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 707 Td (The DNS records for both names have a TTL of 60 seconds. Clients that honour the TTL will reach) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 694 Td (euc1 within about one minute of the DNS switch. Some customer networks run caching resolvers) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 681 Td (that ignore short TTLs; these clients reconnect as their caches expire, which in past drills) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 668 Td (has taken up to 20 minutes for a small tail of sites.) Tj ET
BT /F2 11 Tf 54 645 Td (Gateway buffering) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 623 Td (TS-4 gateways store readings in their local store-and-forward buffer when they cannot reach) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 610 Td (TesseraCloud, so readings are not lost during a failover. After the DNS switch they reconnect) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 597 Td (to euc1 and replay the buffered data in order. Gateways running gateway firmware 5.0.0 or later) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 584 Td (use jittered reconnect backoff and paced replay \(added after INC-2024-031, action item AI-3\).) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 571 Td (Gateways on older 4.x firmware reconnect immediately and replay at full speed, which can) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 558 Td (overload tc-ingest in the first 30 minutes after the switch. The firmware distribution report) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 545 Td (in the TesseraCloud admin console \(Fleet, Firmware\) shows how many gateways are still below) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 532 Td (5.0.0; at the last review in June 2025 this was under 4 percent of the fleet.) Tj ET
BT /F2 13 Tf 54 507 Td (5. Prerequisites) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 485 Td (Before starting the procedure, the Operator confirms the following. Most of these are standing) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 472 Td (conditions that are checked monthly by the Platform team, but they must be reconfirmed during) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 459 Td (an incident.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 437 Td (- Access to the tcctl command line tool at version 2.14 or later, authenticated with a) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 424 Td (   production break-glass role. Run tcctl version to check.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 411 Td (- VPN access to the Meridian management network, or access through the cloud bastion if the) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 398 Td (   corporate VPN is affected.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 385 Td (- Access to the Forge \(CI/CD\) administration console to freeze deployments.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 372 Td (- Access to the status page administration for status.tesseracloud.meridian-instruments.com.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 359 Td (- The incident channel is open in the chat tool and a bridge call is running.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 346 Td (- A Beacon incident ticket exists in category SEC-INCIDENT or INC-PLATFORM \(whichever the) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 333 Td (   service desk used when opening the incident\); the ticket number is posted in the incident) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 320 Td (   channel.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 307 Td (- The euc1 capacity reservation is active. This is confirmed by the monthly DR readiness) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 294 Td (   check; if the check has failed in the last 30 days, the Operator must warn the IC that) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 281 Td (   scale-up may be slower.) Tj ET
BT /F2 13 Tf 54 265 Td (6. Failover procedure) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 243 Td (Record the start time of each step in the incident channel. Steps are numbered continuously) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 230 Td (across all phases so that they can be referenced from postmortems and other runbooks.) Tj ET
BT /F2 11 Tf 54 207 Td (Phase A: Assess and declare) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 185 Td (1. The IC declares or upgrades the incident to SEV1 and announces on the bridge that a) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 172 Td (   regional failover is being considered. The Scribe starts the timeline.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 159 Td (2. The Operator runs tcctl status --region euw1 and posts the output to the incident channel.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 146 Td (   Note which components report DEGRADED or DOWN.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 133 Td (3. The Operator runs tcctl status --region euc1 to confirm the DR region is healthy. All) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 120 Td (   components should report STANDBY or READY. If any euc1 component reports DOWN, stop and) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 107 Td (   escalate to the Head of Platform Engineering before continuing.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 94 Td (4. The Operator checks the tc-ingest health endpoint /healthz on port 8081 in both regions) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 81 Td (   through the internal load balancers. In euw1 this confirms whether ingestion is truly) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 68 Td (   down; in euc1 it should return status ok with mode standby.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 55 Td (5. The IC reviews the decision criteria in section 2 with the Approver. If the decision is to) Tj ET
endstream
endobj
