10 0 obj
<< /Length 5438 >>
stream
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 729 Td (   fail over, the IC states on the bridge: failover approved, approver name, time. The Scribe) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 716 Td (   records this.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 703 Td (6. The Communications lead posts an initial notice on) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 690 Td (   status.tesseracloud.meridian-instruments.com. The first status page update must be) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 677 Td (   published within 30 minutes of the SEV1 declaration, and further updates every 30 minutes) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 664 Td (   until the incident is resolved.) Tj ET
BT /F2 11 Tf 54 650 Td (Phase B: Precheck and freeze) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 628 Td (7. The Operator freezes production deployments for TesseraCloud in Forge by enabling the) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 615 Td (   deployment freeze flag on the tesseracloud-prod environment. This prevents pipelines from) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 602 Td (   deploying to either region during the failover. Post a screenshot or the Forge audit entry) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 589 Td (   in the channel.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 576 Td (8. The Operator runs tcctl failover precheck --target euc1. The precheck validates) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 563 Td (   credentials, DNS zone access, database replica state, MirrorMaker 2 status and euc1) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 550 Td (   capacity. It prints a summary table and exits with PASS, WARN or FAIL. Continue on PASS.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 537 Td (   On WARN, read each warning aloud on the bridge; the IC decides whether to continue. On) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 524 Td (   FAIL, do not continue until the failure is resolved or the IC and Approver explicitly) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 511 Td (   accept the risk.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 498 Td (9. The Kafka lead checks the consumer lag of consumer group tc-stream-prd in euw1 \(tcctl) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 485 Td (   kafka lag --group tc-stream-prd --region euw1\). Record the total lag and the per-partition) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 472 Td (   maximum. A large lag means processed data in TimescaleDB is behind raw data in Kafka,) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 459 Td (   which affects how much reprocessing euc1 will need after promotion. This check was) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 446 Td (   introduced as action item AI-2 of postmortem INC-2024-031, the May 2024 ingestion outage;) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 433 Td (   at that time it was a RabbitMQ queue-depth check, and it was converted to a Kafka consumer) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 420 Td (   lag check after the migration to Kafka under ADR-019.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 407 Td (10. If euw1 is still partially reachable, the Operator stops new MQTT connections to euw1 by) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 394 Td (   setting tc-ingest to drain mode \(tcctl ingest drain --region euw1\). Gateways that lose) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 381 Td (   their connection will start buffering locally. If euw1 is unreachable, skip this step and) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 368 Td (   note it in the channel.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 355 Td (11. The Database lead checks replication status on tsdb-dr-01.euc1.tessera.meridian.internal) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 342 Td (   and records the replay lag reported by the replica. In normal operation it is under 2) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 329 Td (   seconds.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 316 Td (12. The Kafka lead confirms MirrorMaker 2 connectors are running for all replicated topics,) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 303 Td (   including tessera.telemetry.raw, tessera.telemetry.agg and tessera.alerts. Any stopped) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 290 Td (   connector must be noted; its topic may have a larger gap.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 277 Td (13. The Operator scales up euc1 stateless services to production capacity using tcctl scale) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 264 Td (   --region euc1 --profile production. This takes 5 to 10 minutes and can run in parallel) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 251 Td (   with the next steps. Do not proceed to DNS switch until the scale-up has completed.) Tj ET
BT /F2 11 Tf 54 237 Td (Phase C: Promote data tier) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 215 Td (14. The Kafka lead confirms that MirrorMaker 2 replication lag, reported as the metric) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 202 Td (   replication-latency-ms-max, is below 30 seconds \(30000 ms\) for all replicated topics) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 189 Td (   before promotion proceeds. If the lag is above 30 seconds, wait up to 10 minutes and) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 176 Td (   re-check, because lag usually falls quickly once euw1 producers have stopped. If the lag) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 163 Td (   is still above 30 seconds after 10 minutes, the Incident Commander may decide to accept) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 150 Td (   the resulting data loss, provided it stays within the 5-minute RPO, and must record that) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 137 Td (   decision, the observed lag and the time in the incident channel. If the lag suggests loss) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 124 Td (   beyond the RPO, the IC must inform the Approver and the Communications lead before) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 111 Td (   continuing.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 98 Td (15. The Database lead confirms that the DR replica has replayed all WAL it has received and) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 85 Td (   that no further WAL is arriving from euw1.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 72 Td (16. The Operator runs tcctl failover promote --region euc1 --confirm. This command promotes) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 59 Td (   tsdb-dr-01 to primary, switches the euc1 Kafka cluster from replica mode to active mode,) Tj ET
endstream
endobj
